</li>
<li data-start="769" data-end="862" class="">
<p data-start="771" data-end="862" class="">Thus, <strong data-start="777" data-end="826">phonological feasibility is a hard constraint</strong> on what becomes a persistent token.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start="864" data-end="921" class=""><strong data-start="869" data-end="921">2. Phonologization Collapses Latent Alternatives</strong></h4>
<ul data-start="922" data-end="1305">
<li data-start="922" data-end="1011" class="">
<p data-start="924" data-end="1011" class="">A rich latent conceptual field is <strong data-start="958" data-end="972">compressed</strong> into the linear, pronounceable stream.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1012" data-end="1140" class="">
<p data-start="1014" data-end="1140" class="">This requires <strong data-start="1028" data-end="1066">disambiguation and decision-making</strong>: choosing between overlapping meanings, rhythms, or grammatical pathways.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1141" data-end="1305" class="">
<p data-start="1143" data-end="1305" class="">Every word written is a <strong data-start="1167" data-end="1188">lossy compression</strong>â€”a choice that <strong data-start="1203" data-end="1236">rejects multiple alternatives</strong> in favor of <strong data-start="1249" data-end="1304">cultural regularities and physical pronounceability</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start="1307" data-end="1353" class=""><strong data-start="1312" data-end="1353">3. Language as a Binary Decision Tree</strong></h4>
<ul data-start="1354" data-end="1690">
<li data-start="1354" data-end="1601" class="">
<p data-start="1356" data-end="1413" class="">The process of articulating a sentence can be modeled as:</p>
<ul data-start="1416" data-end="1601">
<li data-start="1416" data-end="1504" class="">
<p data-start="1418" data-end="1504" class="">A <strong data-start="1420" data-end="1444">binary decision tree</strong>, where each node is a yes/no about sound, syntax, or sense.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1507" data-end="1601" class="">
<p data-start="1509" data-end="1601" class="">Multiple branches may be pruned <strong data-start="1541" data-end="1559">simultaneously</strong> at a given levelâ€”i.e., <strong data-start="1583" data-end="1600">node collapse</strong>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1602" data-end="1690" class="">
<p data-start="1604" data-end="1690" class="">This produces a <strong data-start="1620" data-end="1642">plausible sequence</strong>, but masks the branching uncertainty behind it.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start="1692" data-end="1758" class=""><strong data-start="1697" data-end="1758">4. The Constraint of Pronounceability Preserves Structure</strong></h4>
<ul data-start="1759" data-end="2081">
<li data-start="1759" data-end="1961" class="">
<p data-start="1761" data-end="1852" class="">The need to <strong data-start="1773" data-end="1798">physically articulate</strong> a token limits the <strong data-start="1818" data-end="1851">expressive degrees of freedom</strong>:</p>
<ul data-start="1855" data-end="1961">
<li data-start="1855" data-end="1925" class="">
<p data-start="1857" data-end="1925" class="">You can't easily encode simultaneity, gesture, or spatial intuition.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1928" data-end="1961" class="">
<p data-start="1930" data-end="1961" class="">You must <strong data-start="1939" data-end="1952">linearize</strong> thought.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1962" data-end="2081" class="">
<p data-start="1964" data-end="2081" class="">This constraint makes language <strong data-start="1995" data-end="2027">archivable and transmittable</strong>, but also <strong data-start="2038" data-end="2052">sterilizes</strong> much of the embodied nuance.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2083" data-end="2086" class="">
<h3 data-start="2088" data-end="2108" class=""><strong data-start="2092" data-end="2108">Implications</strong></h3>
<div class="_tableContainer_16hzy_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="_tableWrapper_16hzy_14 group flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="2110" data-end="2685" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="2110" data-end="2134"><tr data-start="2110" data-end="2134"><th data-start="2110" data-end="2119" data-col-size="sm">Domain</th><th data-start="2119" data-end="2134" data-col-size="lg">Consequence</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="2160" data-end="2685"><tr data-start="2160" data-end="2249"><td data-start="2160" data-end="2176" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2162" data-end="2175">Semiotics</strong></td><td data-start="2176" data-end="2249" data-col-size="lg">Tokens are shadows of gesture, reified for phonological tractability.</td></tr><tr data-start="2250" data-end="2377"><td data-start="2250" data-end="2282" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2252" data-end="2281">Computational Linguistics</strong></td><td data-start="2282" data-end="2377" data-col-size="lg">All language is a compression of a higher-dimensional latent space into pronounceable code.</td></tr><tr data-start="2378" data-end="2528"><td data-start="2378" data-end="2392" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2380" data-end="2391">AI/LLMs</strong></td><td data-start="2392" data-end="2528" data-col-size="lg">Tokenization mimics this ancestral bottleneck: discretizing probabilistic meaning into a fixed vocabulary shaped by breath and time.</td></tr><tr data-start="2529" data-end="2685"><td data-start="2529" data-end="2553" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="2531" data-end="2552">Cognitive Science</strong></td><td data-start="2553" data-end="2685" data-col-size="lg">Decisions in language are structured like <strong data-start="2597" data-end="2640">binary pruning over ambiguous manifolds</strong>, echoing perceptual decision-making trees.</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky end-(--thread-content-margin) h-0 self-end select-none"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 32.7031px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button class="bg-token-bg-primary hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon-md-heavy"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M7 5C7 3.34315 8.34315 2 10 2H19C20.6569 2 22 3.34315 22 5V14C22 15.6569 20.6569 17 19 17H17V19C17 20.6569 15.6569 22 14 22H5C3.34315 22 2 20.6569 2 19V10C2 8.34315 3.34315 7 5 7H7V5ZM9 7H14C15.6569 7 17 8.34315 17 10V15H19C19.5523 15 20 14.5523 20 14V5C20 4.44772 19.5523 4 19 4H10C9.44772 4 9 4.44772 9 5V7ZM5 9C4.44772 9 4 9.44772 4 10V19C4 19.5523 4.44772 20 5 20H14C14.5523 20 15 19.5523 15 19V10C15 9.44772 14.5523 9 14 9H5Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></button></span></div></div></div></div>
