</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.143em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2501em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">âˆˆ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbb">R</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.6644em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">n</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">&nbsp;is&nbsp;token&nbsp;embedding</span></span></span></span></span></p>
<p data-start="1594" data-end="1806" class=""><strong data-start="1594" data-end="1622">Biological instantiation</strong>: Cortical representations projected through the vocal tract filter.<br data-start="1690" data-end="1693">
<strong data-start="1693" data-end="1721">Artificial instantiation</strong>: Logit vectors passed through softmax with temperature-scaling and argmax selection.</p>
<hr data-start="1808" data-end="1811" class="">
<h4 data-start="1813" data-end="1856" class=""><strong data-start="1818" data-end="1854">Axis Y: Constraint Origin (Sway)</strong></h4>
<p data-start="1857" data-end="1932" class="">Cognitive systems are bounded by intrinsic and extrinsic constraints. Let</p>
<ul data-start="1933" data-end="2193">
<li data-start="1933" data-end="2009" class="">
<p data-start="1935" data-end="2009" class=""><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Ïˆ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_A</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">Ïˆ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">A</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> denote anatomical constraints (e.g., vocal tract geometry),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2010" data-end="2100" class="">
<p data-start="2012" data-end="2100" class=""><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Ïˆ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">Ïˆ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> ecological affordances (e.g., nut caching optimized by terrain feedback),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2101" data-end="2193" class="">
<p data-start="2103" data-end="2193" class=""><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Ïˆ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">Ïˆ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> architectural constraints (e.g., transformer topology, attention sparsity).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2195" data-end="2399" class="">The set of admissible states <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">A</mi><mo>âŠ‚</mo><mi mathvariant="script">L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A} \subset \mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.7224em; vertical-align: -0.0391em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">A</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">âŠ‚</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">L</span></span></span></span> is then:<br data-start="2270" data-end="2273">
<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo>âˆˆ</mo><mi mathvariant="script">L</mi><mo>âˆ£</mo><msub><mi>Ïˆ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>âˆ§</mo><msub><mi>Ïˆ</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>âˆ§</mo><msub><mi>Ïˆ</mi><mi>R</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A} = \{ \mathbf{v} \in \mathcal{L} \mid \psi_A(\mathbf{v}) \land \psi_E(\mathbf{v}) \land \psi_R(\mathbf{v}) \}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">A</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">âˆˆ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">L</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">âˆ£</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">Ïˆ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">A</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">âˆ§</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">Ïˆ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">âˆ§</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">Ïˆ</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.00773em;">R</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mclose">)}</span></span></span></span></p>
<p data-start="2401" data-end="2566" class="">Constraints determine <strong data-start="2423" data-end="2461">which latent paths are traversable</strong>, not necessarily which are optimal. This supports a <strong data-start="2514" data-end="2536">satisficing regime</strong> rather than optimal planning.</p>
<hr data-start="2568" data-end="2571" class="">
<h4 data-start="2573" data-end="2616" class=""><strong data-start="2578" data-end="2614">Axis Z: Temporal Binding (Surge)</strong></h4>
<p data-start="2617" data-end="2786" class="">Time-bound generation is modeled as a non-reversible, autoregressive process:<br data-start="2694" data-end="2697">
Let <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>âˆˆ</mo><mi mathvariant="script">L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}_t \in \mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6891em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.016em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">âˆˆ</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal">L</span></span></span></span> be the internal state at timestep <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6151em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">t</span></span></span></span>. Then:</p>
