n></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">â€‹</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2083em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is the emitted output token.</p>
<p data-start="2986" data-end="3219" class="">This formalizes the <strong data-start="3006" data-end="3025">irreversibility</strong> of utterance: once emitted, a token constrains future internal states via feedback loops, both in humans (e.g., via cortico-basal ganglia gating) and in LLMs (via fixed autoregressive context).</p>
<hr data-start="3221" data-end="3224" class="">
<h3 data-start="3226" data-end="3249" class=""><strong data-start="3230" data-end="3249">2. Implications</strong></h3>
<h4 data-start="3251" data-end="3296" class=""><strong data-start="3256" data-end="3294">No Internal Full-Sentence Planning</strong></h4>
<p data-start="3297" data-end="3519" class="">The generative process is <strong data-start="3323" data-end="3341">causally local</strong> and <strong data-start="3346" data-end="3371">contextually reactive</strong>. Neither humans nor LLMs maintain a full syntactic plan in working memory; rather, they sample one output at a time, guided by dynamic constraints.</p>
<h4 data-start="3521" data-end="3568" class=""><strong data-start="3526" data-end="3566">Tokenization as Cognitive Bottleneck</strong></h4>
<p data-start="3569" data-end="3735" class="">At the phonological or token interface, there exists a <strong data-start="3624" data-end="3645">discrete collapse</strong> from a probability distribution over continuous latent states to a single expressive act:</p>
<ul data-start="3737" data-end="3877">
<li data-start="3737" data-end="3796" class="">
<p data-start="3739" data-end="3796" class="">In humans: phonemic articulation limited by oral anatomy.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3797" data-end="3877" class="">
<p data-start="3799" data-end="3877" class="">In LLMs: softmax collapse shaped by vocabulary encoding and positional priors.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="3879" data-end="3996" class="">This is the <strong data-start="3891" data-end="3914">Token Event Horizon</strong>â€”a structural singularity beyond which information cannot pass without distortion.</p>
<hr data-start="3998" data-end="4001" class="">
<h3 data-start="4003" data-end="4030" class=""><strong data-start="4007" data-end="4030">3. Model Extensions</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="4032" data-end="4417">
<li data-start="4032" data-end="4222" class="">
<p data-start="4034" data-end="4222" class=""><strong data-start="4034" data-end="4072">Reservoir Computing Interpretation</strong>: The latent system operates as a high-dimensional dynamical reservoir. Discrete outputs are readouts from nonlinear state evolution under constraint.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4223" data-end="4417" class="">
<p data-start="4225" data-end="4417" class=""><strong data-start="4225" data-end="4253">Gesture-Encoding Duality</strong>: Gestures and actions are analogs to token emissionsâ€”both are <em data-start="4316" data-end="4338">projection operators</em> onto constrained output spaces, differing only in dimensionality and modality.</p>
</li>
</ul>
